description:
Design a circuit that functions as a decoder, converting specific 8-bit input values to designated 8-bit output values. The module takes an 8-bit input (`dataIn`) and maps it to a predetermined output (`dataOut`) based on a case structure: it converts 8'h1D to 8'd87, 8'h1B to 8'd83, 8'h1C to 8'd65, and 8'h23 to 8'd68, while mapping any other input value to 0. This structure allows for the selective translation of input signals into unique output values, effectively encoding a small set of instructions or commands.
module top_module(
	input [7:0] dataIn,
	output [7:0] dataOut
);

code:
module top_module(
	input [7:0] dataIn,
	output [7:0] dataOut
);reg [7:0] data;
  always @ (dataIn) begin     
    case(dataIn)
      8'h1D    : data = 8'd87;     
      8'h1B    : data = 8'd83;
		8'h1C    : data = 8'd65;
		8'h23    : data = 8'd68;
      default  : data = 0;     
    endcase
  end

  assign dataOut = data;

endmodule

