Design a dual-function D flip-flop (DFF) with asynchronous reset (R) and set (S) controls. The output Q captures the value of input D at the negative edge of the clock signal C, unless reset is asserted (R=0), which sets Q to LOW, or set is asserted (S=1), which sets Q to HIGH. The module includes timing specifications for different FPGA architectures, ensuring proper setup and hold times for D and R signals with respect to the clock edge.
