Design an Automatic Gain Control (AGC) circuit that dynamically adjusts the amplitude of an input signal based on a control signal. The module takes a 16-bit input signal and an 8-bit control signal to determine the appropriate gain value, which can range from no adjustment to maximum increase or reduction. Based on the specified control signal, the gain value is computed using a function, and the adjusted signal is output after multiplying the input signal by the derived gain. This design is particularly useful in audio processing or communication systems, ensuring consistent output levels despite varying input amplitudes.
